    apply: { situation: ['Listen to the friends before they board. Find the mistake and how they check the train.', '乗車前の四人の会話を聞きましょう。間違いと、電車を確認する方法を聞き取りましょう。'], text: '<p><strong>Emma:</strong> Leo, is this the right train for Inari?<br><strong>Leo:</strong> I think so. Let\'s get on.<br><strong>Nao:</strong> Wait! This sign shows a different destination. We need the other platform.<br><strong>Leo:</strong> Oh, you\'re right. Let\'s check with the staff first.<br><strong>Emma:</strong> Good idea. I don\'t want our adventure to start on the wrong train!</p>', questions: [['Do they get on the wrong train?', 'No. Nao notices before they board.'], ['What does Nao check?', 'The sign/destination.'], ['Where do they need to go?', 'The other platform.'], ['Who will they ask to confirm?', 'The station staff.']] },
    choose: [['Which platform (should / are) we use?', 'should'], ['Is this the (right / write) train?', 'right'], ['We need to (change / changing) trains.', 'change'], ['Please check before you (board / boarded).', 'board'], ['Two tickets (to / on) Inari, please.', 'to'], ['Let\'s get (off / of) here.', 'off']],
    choices: [['"Wait! Not this train. Use the other platform." Where should they go?', 'The other platform', 'Onto this train', 'A'], ['"Two tickets, please." How many tickets does the speaker want?', 'One', 'Two', 'B'], ['"No change is needed." Do the travelers need to change trains?', 'Yes', 'No', 'B'], ['"Ask the staff before boarding." What should they do first?', 'Ask the staff', 'Board immediately', 'A']],
    mission: { situation: ['At a practice station counter, Emma listens to the staff. Your tutor reads the short exchange, then plays Leo. All ticket and journey details in this exercise are fictional practice information.', '練習用の駅の窓口でエマが係員の説明を聞きます。講師は短い会話を読んでからレオ役になります。この練習の切符や移動の情報は架空の設定です。'], task: ['Listen for the number and type of tickets, whether a change is needed, and what to check before boarding. Tell Leo the details and ask for repetition if needed.', '切符の枚数と種類、乗り換えの有無、乗車前に確認することを聞き取り、レオに伝えましょう。必要なら繰り返してもらいましょう。'], roles: ['Leo', 'Emma'], text: '<p><strong>Emma:</strong> Two adult tickets to Inari, please. One-way.<br><strong>Staff:</strong> Certainly. You do not need to change trains. Please check the destination on the board before you get on.<br><strong>Emma:</strong> Is there a ticket machine near here?<br><strong>Staff:</strong> Yes, beside the information desk. Ask us again if you need help.</p>', lines: ['Emma, what tickets did you ask for?', 'Are they one-way or return tickets?', 'Do we need to change trains?', 'What should we check before we get on?', 'Where is the ticket machine?'], evidence: 'Two adult one-way tickets, no change, check destination board, machine beside information desk. Repeat requested parts. Do not ask for a real fare, platform number, or timetable; these are not supplied.', useful: ['We need ... tickets.', 'They are one-way / return tickets.', 'We do not need to ...', 'The staff said ...', 'Could you repeat that, please?'] },
    topics: [['TRAIN TRAVEL', ['Do you often travel by train?', 'What do you check before boarding?', 'What do you like about train journeys?']], ['ASKING FOR HELP', ['Who would you ask at a station?', 'What question would you ask?', 'What would you do if you did not understand?']], ['TRAVEL MISTAKES', ['Have you ever gone the wrong way?', 'How did you notice?', 'What helped you solve it?']]],
    trivia: ['British English often uses "return ticket" for a trip there and back. American English often uses "round-trip ticket." "One-way ticket" is commonly understood for travel in one direction.', '往復の切符は、イギリス英語では return ticket、アメリカ英語では round-trip ticket とよく言います。one-way ticket は片道の切符を表す言い方として広く使われます。'], triviaQuestion: ['Does a return ticket include the journey back?', 'Yes.'],
